items.proof:
Let $\xi_n$ be the unique element of $\partial\sigma_{A(0)}((x_{n+2} - x_{n+1})/\lambda_n)$ such that:
$$
\begin{array}{l}
d\bigl(-(x_{n+2} - 2x_{n+1} + x_n)/\lambda_n^2 - \nabla f(x_{n+2}), \partial\sigma_{A(0)}((x_{n+2} - x_{n+1})/\lambda_n)\bigr) \\
= \left| \xi_n + (x_{n+2} - 2x_{n+1} + x_n)/\lambda_n^2 + \nabla f(x_{n+2}) \right|.
\end{array}
$$
From the definitions of the term $\xi_n$ and the sequence $(x_n)$, we have:
$$
\begin{array}{l}
\left| \xi_n + (x_{n+2} - 2x_{n+1} + x_n)/\lambda_n^2 + \nabla f(x_{n+2}) \right| \\
\leqslant e\big(A((x_{n+2} - x_{n+1})/\lambda_n), \partial\sigma_{A(0)}((x_{n+2} - x_{n+1})/\lambda_n)\big). \tag{24}
\end{array}
$$
Since $s-\lim_{n \to +\infty} x_{n+2} - x_{n+1} = 0$ and the sequence $(\lambda_n)$ is minorized by some $\underline{\lambda} > 0$, we infer from condition (22) that the right member of inequality (24) tends to $0$ when $n \to +\infty$. Since $s-\lim_{n \to +\infty} x_{n+2} - 2x_{n+1} + x_n = 0$ and $s-\lim_{n \to +\infty} \nabla f(x_{n+2}) = \nabla f(x_\infty)$, we deduce from inequality (24) that $s-\lim_{n \to +\infty} \xi_n = -\nabla f(x_\infty)$. On the other hand, the fact that $\xi_n \in \partial\sigma_{A(0)}((x_{n+2} - x_{n+1})/\lambda_n)$ is equivalent to $x_{n+2} - x_{n+1} \in N_{A(0)}(\xi_n)$. Finally, what remains to be seen is that $N_{A(0)}(\xi_n) \subset N_{A(0)}(-\nabla f(x_\infty))$ for $n$ large enough. Since $A(0)$ is a convex polyhedron, it suffices to apply property (21) with $C := A(0)$ and $\overline{x} := -\nabla f(x_\infty)$.
